{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1353,
 "dur": 45.091,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Every night, the Whisker brothers gave the king's gold coins a haircut.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.252
  },
  {
   "text": "One tiny shave per coin. Get caught: forty years scrubbing the royal moat.",
   "s": 3.452,
   "e": 7.232
  },
  {
   "text": "The gold dust went into a jar labelled \"PICKLES.\"",
   "s": 7.432,
   "e": 9.762
  },
  {
   "text": "But by spring, the coins had shrunk. A loaf of bread cost two coins and a button.",
   "s": 9.882,
   "e": 14.01
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the king's face on the coins lost his crown. Then his ears. Then his nose.",
   "s": 14.21,
   "e": 18.259
  },
  {
   "text": "King Barnaby's fix: make every coin twice as big. The brothers bought bigger files.",
   "s": 18.459,
   "e": 22.873
  },
  {
   "text": "Soon coins were the size of dinner plates, and shaved into stars.",
   "s": 23.073,
   "e": 25.816
  },
  {
   "text": "So how do you catch a haircut nobody can see?",
   "s": 26.016,
   "e": 28.207
  },
  {
   "text": "Mina from the mint pressed tiny lines all around every coin's edge.",
   "s": 28.707,
   "e": 32.034
  },
  {
   "text": "Shave a coin now, and the lines vanish. One bald spot.",
   "s": 32.234,
   "e": 35.011
  },
  {
   "text": "Like a birthday cake with one slice gone: everybody notices.",
   "s": 35.211,
   "e": 38.41
  },
  {
   "text": "The baker felt one coin's edge and blew his whistle.",
   "s": 38.61,
   "e": 40.878
  },
  {
   "text": "The Whisker brothers still give haircuts. To the royal sheep.",
   "s": 41.078,
   "e": 43.791
  }
 ],
